note S1: a function name of 9..63 bytes whose first 8 bytes spell an 8-byte keyword (continue, truncate)
note is a name, not that keyword: defined, called in a value, called as a statement, two of them told
note apart in full. Exit 0, else the failing check's number.
om2
fn continue_x a long to long
ret add a 1
end
fn continue_y a long to long
ret add a 2
end
fn truncate_it to void
ret
end
fn main to int
x = continue_x 3
if ne x 4
ret 1
end
y = continue_y 10
if ne y 12
ret 2
end
truncate_it
ret 0
end
